{"name":"Hassan II Mosque","hex":"#009e6d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mosque","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place of worship for Muslims, often having at least one minaret; a masjid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mosque"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hassan II Mosque","blocks":[{"text":"The Hassan II Mosque is a mosque in Casablanca, Morocco. It is the second largest mosque in Africa and one of the largest mosques in the world. Its minaret is the world's second tallest minaret at 210 metres (689 ft). Completed in 1993, it was designed by Michel Pinseau under the guidance of King Hassan II and built by Moroccan artisans from all over the kingdom. The minaret is 60 stories high, topped by a laser, the light from which is directed towards Mecca. The mosque stands on a promontory looking out to the Atlantic Ocean; worshippers can pray over the sea but there is no glass floor looking into the sea. The walls are made of handcrafted marble, and the roof is retractable. A maximum of 105,000 worshippers can gather together for prayer: 25,000 inside the mosque hall and another 80,000 on the mosque's outside ground."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/Hassan_II_mosque%2C_Casablanca_2.jpg/330px-Hassan_II_mosque%2C_Casablanca_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hassan_II_Mosque","wikidata":"Q41346"},{"title":"Hassan II","blocks":[{"text":"Hassan II was King of Morocco from 1961 until his death in 1999."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Hassan_II_%281983%29.jpg/330px-Hassan_II_%281983%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hassan_II","wikidata":"Q69103"},{"title":"Mosque","blocks":[{"text":"A mosque, also called a masjid, is a place of worship for Muslims. The term usually refers to a covered building, but can be any place where Islamic prayers are performed, such as an outdoor courtyard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Masjid_e_Nabawi_Interior_2.jpg/330px-Masjid_e_Nabawi_Interior_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mosque","wikidata":"Q32815"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Mosquee_Hassan_II_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Mosquee_Hassan_II_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Mosquee_Hassan_II_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Mosquee_Hassan_II_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Mosquee_Hassan_II_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Mosquee_Hassan_II_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of the mosque in Boulevard Sidi Mohammed Ben Abdellah","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMosquee_Hassan_II_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Sunshine_on_mosque_Hassan_II_in_Casablanca%2C_Morocco_-_Flickr_-_Milamber%27s_portfolio.jpg/500px-Sunshine_on_mosque_Hassan_II_in_Casablanca%2C_Morocco_-_Flickr_-_Milamber%27s_portfolio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Sunshine_on_mosque_Hassan_II_in_Casablanca%2C_Morocco_-_Flickr_-_Milamber%27s_portfolio.jpg/1280px-Sunshine_on_mosque_Hassan_II_in_Casablanca%2C_Morocco_-_Flickr_-_Milamber%27s_portfolio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Sunshine_on_mosque_Hassan_II_in_Casablanca%2C_Morocco_-_Flickr_-_Milamber%27s_portfolio.jpg/500px-Sunshine_on_mosque_Hassan_II_in_Casablanc